Rule 1 (tensor-tensor inputs must be broadcast-compatible across all dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 2 (bool tensors are not allowed for tensor-tensor subtraction)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 5 (for integral tensor-tensor inputs, alpha must be an integer-valued number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if ((dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 5)) then v_3 % 1 = 0
>>
Rule 7 (when input tensors have exactly the same shape, out must match that shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_4 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) then (ndim(v_4) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_4, i) = shape(v_1, i))
